WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.594
If for some reason you need to replace
a needle. The process is the same for both

2
00:00:06.794 --> 00:00:11.360
the main bed and the ribber.
First remove the carriage from the bed,

3
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:17.880
Push the sponge bar out as far as
need to, to release the damaged needle.

4
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:25.560
Just an FYI, the sponge bar is also called a needle retaining bar.
That makes sense, no?

5
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.640
And this is a good time to check
the condition of your sponge bar.

6
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.080
Lift up on the butt of the needle
and lift it out of the slot.

7
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.400
Pull the needle out
of the slot and toss it.

8
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.760
Replace it with a new needle in reverse.

9
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:56.360
Hold the needle by the butt,
insert the hook into the slot until it clears at the back and then
drop it into place.

10
00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:01.440
Then replaced the sponge bar
back into position.

11
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.280
If that sponge bar is flat,
get one ordered and get it replaced.

12
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.880
One trick that many knitters use is

13
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.200
to borrow needles from the ends
of the needle bet as a temporary

14
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.320
replacement until you
can order more needles.

